[?2004h[?1049h[22;0;0t[1;36r(B[m[4l[?7h[39;49m[?1h=[?1h=[?25l[39;49m(B[m[H[2J[34;77H(B[0;7m[ Reading... ](B[m[34;75H(B[0;7m[ Read 140 lines ](B[m[H(B[0;7m  GNU nano 4.8                                                                  FINDINGS.md                                                                            [1;166H(B[m[35d(B[0;7m^G(B[m Get Help     (B[0;7m^O(B[m Write Out    (B[0;7m^W(B[m Where Is     (B[0;7m^K(B[m Cut Text     (B[0;7m^J(B[m Justify[81G(B[0;7m^C(B[m Cur Pos[97G(B[0;7mM-U(B[m Undo[35;113H(B[0;7mM-A(B[m Mark Text   (B[0;7mM-](B[m To Bracket  (B[0;7mM-Q(B[m Previous[36d(B[0;7m^X(B[m Exit[36;17H(B[0;7m^R(B[m Read File    (B[0;7m^\(B[m Replace[49G(B[0;7m^U(B[m Paste Text   (B[0;7m^T(B[m To Spell     (B[0;7m^_(B[m Go To Line   (B[0;7mM-E(B[m Redo[36;113H(B[0;7mM-6(B[m Copy Text   (B[0;7m^Q(B[m Where Was    (B[0;7mM-W(B[m Next[34d[2d[39;49m[36m# Findings — Part 4 debug lab[4d[39m(B[mFill in one entry per defect you find. Paste the *actual* output you saw —[5dwe cross-check it against your session recording and your git diff, and the[6ddiagnostic path matters more to us than the fix itself.[8dBefore you start investigating, begin recording:[9d`script -q part4-session.log` (or `asciinema rec part4-session.cast`), and[10dcommit that file alongside this one.[12d---[14d[36m## Defect 1[16d[39m(B[m**Symptom:**[18dWhen I ran `./scenario.sh up`, the migration Job failed with this error:[20d```[21dJob.batch "migrate" is invalid: spec.template.spec.restartPolicy: Required value: valid values: "OnFailure", "Never"[22d```[24d**Cause:**[26dThe migrate Job's `restartPolicy` was set to `Always` at line 16 of `broken-chart/templates/migrate-job.yaml`. Kubernetes Jobs only accept `Never` or `OnFailure`, so (B[0;7m>[28;1H(B[m**Fix:**[30dChanged the value in `broken-chart/templates/migrate-job.yaml`:[32d- Before: `restartPolicy: Always`[33d- After: `restartPolicy: Never`[2d[?12l[?25h[?25l[6d[?12l[?25h[?25l[11d[?12l[?25h[?25l[16d[?12l[?25h[?25l[23d[?12l[?25h[?25l[34d[K[28d[?12l[?25h[?25l[30d[?12l[?25h[?25l[2;34r[34;1H
[1;36r[33;1H[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[4S[1;36r[30;1HI chose `Never` because each retry creates a new pod, instead of restarting the same container. The number of retries is controlled by `backoffLimit`.[32d**How I found it:**[33d[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[5S[1;36r[29;1H1. Ran `./scenario.sh up` and got the migrate Job error.[30d2. Read the error message, which named `restartPolicy` and listed the valid values.[31d3. Ran `cat -n broken-chart/templates/migrate-job.yaml` to see the file with line numbers.[32d4. Found the wrong value on line 16 and changed it from `Always` to `Never`.[33d5. Confirmed the change with `grep -n restartPolicy broken-chart/templates/migrate-job.yaml`.[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[2S[1;36r[32;1H---[33d[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1H[36m## Defect 2[39m(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[2S[1;36r[33;1H**Symptom:**[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1H[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[3S[1;36r[31;1HAfter deploying the lab, I ran `kubectl -n debug-lab get pods`. All app pods and the migrate Job were stuck in `CreateContainerConfigError`. The events showed this er(B[0;7m>[33;1H(B[m```[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1HError: container has runAsNonRoot and image has non-numeric user (nonroot), cannot verify user is non-root[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1H```[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1H[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[3S[1;36r[31;1H**Cause:**[33dThe Helm templates set `runAsNonRoot: true` but did not set a numeric user ID. The image's user is the name `nonroot`, which is UID `65532`. Kubernetes needs a number(B[0;7m>[33;1H(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[8S[1;36r[27;1H**Fix:**[29dI added `runAsUser: 65532` under `runAsNonRoot: true` in six templates: `backend.yaml`, `gateway.yaml`, `worker.yaml`, `reporter.yaml`, `metrics.yaml` and `migrate-jo(B[0;7m>[31;1H(B[mBefore:[33d```[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[14S[1;36r[20;1HrunAsNonRoot: true[21d```[23dAfter:[25d```[26drunAsNonRoot: true[27drunAsUser: 65532[28d```[30dI used the numeric UID because `runAsUser` needs a number, not a username.[32dI also deleted and recreated the migrate Job, because Kubernetes does not allow changes to an existing Job's pod template. Helm could not update it in place.[33d[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[8S[1;36r[26;1H**How I found it:**[28d1. Ran `kubectl -n debug-lab get pods` and saw `CreateContainerConfigError`.[29d2. Ran `kubectl -n debug-lab get events --sort-by=.lastTimestamp` and found the `runAsNonRoot ... non-numeric user` message.[30d3. Ran `grep -rn -i "runAs\|securityContext" broken-chart/` and saw that each template set `runAsNonRoot` with no user ID.[31d4. Ran `docker pull` and `docker inspect` on the image, which showed its user is `nonroot`.[32d5. Ran `docker create`, `docker cp` and `tar` to read `/etc/passwd` inside the image, which showed `nonroot:x:65532:65532`.[33d6. Added `runAsUser: 65532` to the six templates and checked with `grep -rn runAsUser broken-chart/`, which showed six matches.[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[6S[1;36r[28;1H7. Deleted the old migrate Job with `kubectl -n debug-lab delete job migrate`, then ran `./scenario.sh up`.[29d---[31d[36m## Defect 3[33d[39m(B[m**Symptom:**[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[4S[1;36r[31;1H**Cause:*