.yaml`:[32d- Before: `restartPolicy: Always`[33d- After: `restartPolicy: Never`[2d[?12l[?25h[?25l[6d[?12l[?25h[?25l[12d[?12l[?25h[?25l[16d[?12l[?25h[?25l[21d[?12l[?25h[?25l[27d[?12l[?25h[?25l[34d[K[30d[?12l[?25h[?25l[33d[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[5S[1;36r[30;1HI chose `Never` because each retry creates a new pod, instead of restarting the same container. The number of retries is controlled by `backoffLimit`.[32d**How I found it:**[33d[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[4S[1;36r[30;1H1. Ran `./scenario.sh up` and got the migrate Job error.[31d2. Read the error message, which named `restartPolicy` and listed the valid values.[32d3. Ran `cat -n broken-chart/templates/migrate-job.yaml` to see the file with line numbers.[33d4. Found the wrong value on line 16 and changed it from `Always` to `Never`.[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1H5. Confirmed the change with `grep -n restartPolicy broken-chart/templates/migrate-job.yaml`.[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[2S[1;36r[32;1H---[33d[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1H[36m## Defect 2[39m(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1H[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1H**Symptom:**[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1H[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1HAfter deploying the lab, I ran `kubectl -n debug-lab get pods`. All app pods and the migrate Job were stuck in `CreateContainerConfigError`. The events showed this er(B[0;7m>[33;1H(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1H[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1H```[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1HError: container has runAsNonRoot and image has non-numeric user (nonroot), cannot verify user is non-root[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[2S[1;36r[32;1H```[33d[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[4S[1;36r[30;1H**Cause:**[32dThe Helm templates set `runAsNonRoot: true` but did not set a numeric user ID. The image's user is the name `nonroot`, which is UID `65532`. Kubernetes needs a number(B[0;7m>[33;1H(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[3S[1;36r[31;1H**Fix:**[33dI added `runAsUser: 65532` under `runAsNonRoot: true` in six templates: `backend.yaml`, `gateway.yaml`, `worker.yaml`, `reporter.yaml`, `metrics.yaml` and `migrate-jo(B[0;7m>[33;1H(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[2S[1;36r[33;1HBefore:[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[2S[1;36r[33;1H```[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[3S[1;36r[31;1HrunAsNonRoot: true[32d```[33d[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1HAfter:[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1H[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[3S[1;36r[31;1H```[32drunAsNonRoot: true[33drunAsUser: 65532[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[4S[1;36r[30;1H```[32dI used the numeric UID because `runAsUser` needs a number, not a username.[33d[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[4S[1;36r[30;1HI also deleted and recreated the migrate Job, because Kubernetes does not allow changes to an existing Job's pod template. Helm could not update it in place.[32d**How I found it:**[33d[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[5S[1;36r[29;1H1. Ran `kubectl -n debug-lab get pods` and saw `CreateContainerConfigError`.[30d2. Ran `kubectl -n debug-lab get events --sort-by=.lastTimestamp` and found the `runAsNonRoot ... non-numeric user` message.[31d3. Ran `grep -rn -i "runAs\|securityContext" broken-chart/` and saw that each template set `runAsNonRoot` with no user ID.[32d4. Ran `docker pull` and `docker inspect` on the image, which showed its user is `nonroot`.[33d5. Ran `docker create`, `docker cp` and `tar` to read `/etc/passwd` inside the image, which showed `nonroot:x:65532:65532`.[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[3S[1;36r[31;1H6. Added `runAsUser: 65532` to the six templates and checked with `grep -rn runAsUser broken-chart/`, which showed six matches.[32d7. Deleted the old migrate Job with `kubectl -n debug-lab delete job migrate`, then ran `./scenario.sh up`.[33d---[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[2S[1;36r[33;1H[36m## Defect 3[39m(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[2S[1;36r[33;1H**Symptom:**[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
[1;36r[33;1H[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[2S[1;36r[32;1HThe backend and gateway pods were failing their readiness checks. `kubectl describe pod` showed the probe failing with `connection refused` on port 8080, while the ap(B[0;7m>[33;1H(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[16S[1;36r[18;1H**Cause:**[20dThe chart never set the `PORT` environment variable, so the application used its default port, 8081. The readiness probe and Service were configured for port 8080, so(B[0;7m>[22;1H(B[m**Fix:**[24dI added `PORT: "8080"` under the `env:` block for the backend in `broken-chart/values.yaml`:[26d```[27denv:[28dPORT: "8080"[29d```[31dI chose this over changing the port in the chart because the Service and probes were already set to 8080. Changing the app's port keeps the rest of the configuration (B[0;7m>[33;1H(B[mThe gateway has the same problem and needs the same change. At the time of writing, I had not yet confirmed the gateway fix. This is still in progress.[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[14S[1;36r[21;1H**How I found it:**[23d1. Ran `kubectl -n debug-lab describe pod` and saw the readiness probe failing with `connection refused` on port 8080.[24d2. Ran `kubectl -n debug-lab logs` and saw the app listening on `:8081`.[25d3. Ran `grep -rn -i "port"` on `values.yaml` and `backend.yaml`, which showed the probe using `common.port` (8080) and no `PORT` variable set.[26d4. Added `PORT: "8080"` to the backend's env block, then ran `./scenario.sh up`.[27d5. Confirmed with the backend log (`/healthz -> 200`) and `./scenario.sh verify`, which now passes the backend check.[28d---[30d[36m## Defect 4[32d[39m(B[m**Symptom:**[33d[?12l[?25h[?25l[2d[K[3d**How I found it:**[4d[K[5d1. Ran `kubectl -n debug-lab describe pod` and saw the readiness probe failing with `connection refused` on port 8080.[6d2. Ran `kubectl -n debug-lab logs` and saw the app listening on `:8081`.[K[7d3. Ran `grep -rn -i "port"` on `values.yaml` and `backend.yaml`, which showed the probe using `common.port` (8080) and no `PORT` variable set.[8d4. Added `PORT: "8080"` to the backend's env block, then ran `./scenario.sh up`.[9d5. Confirmed with the backend log (`/healthz -> 200`) and `./scenario.sh verify`, which now passes the backend check.[10d---[K[12d[36m## Defect 4[13d[39m(B[m[K[14d**Symptom:**[K[15d[K[16d**Cause:**[17d[K[18d**Fix:**[19d[K[20d**How I found it:**[21d[K[22d---[23d[K[24d[36m## Defect 5[39m(B[m[K[25d[K[26d**Symptom:**[K[27d[K[28d**Cause:**[30d**Fix:**[K[32;3HHow I found it:**[33d[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[7S[1;36r[27;1H---[29d[36m## Defect 6[31d[39m(B[m**Symptom:**[33d**Cause:**[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[10S[1;36r[25;1H**Fix:**[27d**How I found it:**[29d---[31dIf you ran out of time on any defect, say so here and describe what you would[32dhave tried next — that section is read carefully and counts in your favour.[33d[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[A[?12l[?25h[?25l[A[?12l[?25h[?25l[A[?12l[?25h[?25l[A[?12l[?25h[?25l[A[?12l[?25h[?25l[A[?12l[?25h[?25l[A[?12l[?25h[?25l[A[?12l[?25h[?25l[A[?12l[?25h[?25l[A[?12l[?25h[?25l[A[?12l[?25h[?25l[A[?12l[?25h[?25l[A[?12l[?25h[?25l