.yaml`:[32d- Before: `restartPolicy: Always`[33d- After: `restartPolicy: Never`[2d[?12l[?25h[?25l[7d[?12l[?25h[?25l[24d[?12l[?25h[?25l[34d[K[A[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[4S[1;36r[31;1HI chose `Never` because each retry creates a new pod, instead of restarting the same container. The number of retries is controlled by `backoffLimit`.[33d**How I found it:**[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[9S[1;36r[26;1H1. Ran `./scenario.sh up` and got the migrate Job error.[27d2. Read the error message, which named `restartPolicy` and listed the valid values.[28d3. Ran `cat -n broken-chart/templates/migrate-job.yaml` to see the file with line numbers.[29d4. Found the wrong value on line 16 and changed it from `Always` to `Never`.[30d5. Confirmed the change with `grep -n restartPolicy broken-chart/templates/migrate-job.yaml`.[31d---[33d[36m## Defect 2[39m(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[8S[1;36r[27;1H**Symptom:**[29dAfter deploying the lab, I ran `kubectl -n debug-lab get pods`. All app pods and the migrate Job were stuck in `CreateContainerConfigError`. The events showed this er(B[0;7m>[31;1H(B[m```[32dError: container has runAsNonRoot and image has non-numeric user (nonroot), cannot verify user is non-root[33d```[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[8S[1;36r[27;1H**Cause:**[29dThe Helm templates set `runAsNonRoot: true` but did not set a numeric user ID. The image's user is the name `nonroot`, which is UID `65532`. Kubernetes needs a number(B[0;7m>[31;1H(B[m**Fix:**[33dI added `runAsUser: 65532` under `runAsNonRoot: true` in six templates: `backend.yaml`, `gateway.yaml`, `worker.yaml`, `reporter.yaml`, `metrics.yaml` and `migrate-jo(B[0;7m>[33;1H(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[5S[1;36r[30;1HBefore:[32d```[33drunAsNonRoot: true[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[6S[1;36r[28;1H```[30dAfter:[32d```[33drunAsNonRoot: true[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[9S[1;36r[25;1HrunAsUser: 65532[26d```[28dI used the numeric UID because `runAsUser` needs a number, not a username.[30dI also deleted and recreated the migrate Job, because Kubernetes does not allow changes to an existing Job's pod template. Helm could not update it in place.[32d**How I found it:**[33d[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[4S[1;36r[30;1H1. Ran `kubectl -n debug-lab get pods` and saw `CreateContainerConfigError`.[31d2. Ran `kubectl -n debug-lab get events --sort-by=.lastTimestamp` and found the `runAsNonRoot ... non-numeric user` message.[32d3. Ran `grep -rn -i "runAs\|securityContext" broken-chart/` and saw that each template set `runAsNonRoot` with no user ID.[33d4. Ran `docker pull` and `docker inspect` on the image, which showed its user is `nonroot`.[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[3S[1;36r[31;1H5. Ran `docker create`, `docker cp` and `tar` to read `/etc/passwd` inside the image, which showed `nonroot:x:65532:65532`.[32d6. Added `runAsUser: 65532` to the six templates and checked with `grep -rn runAsUser broken-chart/`, which showed six matches.[33d7. Deleted the old migrate Job with `kubectl -n debug-lab delete job migrate`, then ran `./scenario.sh up`.[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[3S[1;36r[31;1H---[33d[36m## Defect 3[39m(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d[3S[1;36r[32;1H**Symptom:**[33d[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
