er the port fix, the gateway's readiness check failed. The gateway log showed:[24d```[K[25dreadiness failed: backend not reachable: GET http://backend.default.svc:8080/healthz: ... lookup backend.default.svc on 10.96.0.10:53: no such host[27d[K[28d`verify` also reported `gateway /status does not report backend=ok`.[29d[K[30d**Cause:**[31d[K[32dThe gateway's `BACKEND_URL` in `broken-chart/values.yaml` pointed at namespace `default`, but the backend runs in namespace `debug-lab`. DNS couldn't resolve a host i(B[0;7m>[33;1H(B[m[K[?12l[?25h[?25l[16;23r[16;1H[2T[1;36r[6;14r[6;1H[2T[1;36r[2;1H[K[3d**Cause:**[5dThe gateway's `BACKEND_URL` in `broken-chart/values.yaml` pointed at namespace `default`, but the backend runs in namespace `debug-lab`. DNS couldn't resolve a host i[7d**Fix:**[9dI changed the namespace in `BACKEND_URL` from `default` to `debug-lab`, so the value is `http://backend.debug-lab.svc:8080`. I kept the rest of the URL the same, sinc(B[0;7m>[13;30H(B[mlogs <gateway-pod> --tail=5` and saw the `no such host` error.[K[14;5Head the hostname in the error (`backend.default.svc`) and compared it with the namespace the lab runs in (`debug-lab`).[15d3. Ran `grep -n -A6 "^gateway:" broken-chart/values.yaml` and found `BACKEND_URL` on line 39.[K[16d4. Changed the namespace, ran `./scenario.sh up`, then `./scenario.sh verify`. The check `gateway /status reports backend=ok` passed.[20;11H[36m5[24d[39m(B[mThe metrics pod was never created. `kubectl -n debug-lab get events` showed:[25d[K[27dreplicaset/metrics-...  (combined from similar events): Error creating: pods "metrics-..." is forbidden: maximum cpu usage per Container is 1, but limit is 4[28d```[K[32d metrics block in `broken-chart/values.yaml` set a CPU request of `"2"` and a CPU limit of `"4"`. The cluster's LimitRange in `cluster-state/limits.yaml` caps each[33d[?12l[?25h[?25l[20;34r[20;1H[5T[1;36r[2;19r[2;1H[6T[1;36r[3;1HThe m