K[25;30Hlogs <reporter-pod> --tail=3` and saw the parse error.[26;30Hdescribe pod <reporter-pod> | grep -A3 -i "mounts\|serviceaccount"`. The ServiceAccount token is mounted normally.[27;4HChecked `broken-chart/templates/reporter.yaml`. It doesn't set any token, volume or API options; it only loops over `.Values.reporter.env`.[28d[K[29d**What I would try next:**[31d- Find out what settings the reporter app expects in its environment. For example, a namespace variable could be missing, which would make it build a broken API reque(B[0;7m>[32;1H(B[m- Test the API call directly from a pod running as the `reporter` ServiceAccount, to see what the API really returns.[33d- Compare the reporter's env with the other workloads, looking for a setting the reporter needs but doesn't have.[?12l[?25h[?25l[A[?12l[?25h[?25l[30d[?12l[?25h[?25l[29;27H[?12l[?25h[?25l[A[?12l[?25h[?25l[29;27H[?12l[?25h[?25l[31;114H[?12l[?25h[?25l[2;34r[34;1H[2S[1;36r[32;1HIf you ran out of time on any defect, say so here and describe what you would[33dhave tried next — that section is read carefully and counts in your favour.[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[34d
