local`. Risk: credentials or data in transit would be exposed in any real environment. cert-manager would b(B[0;7m>[5;1H(B[m- **No NetworkPolicy.** Any pod can reach the service. Risk: lateral movement from a compromised pod.[6d- **No image vulnerability scan** (the optional Trivy job). Risk: shipping known CVEs in the base image. I pinned the base image tag but did not scan it.[7d- **`setup.sh` smoke check only warns** if the ingress is not reachable, so a re-run can't fail just because the controller is still warming up. Risk: a broken ingres(B[0;7m>[2;112H(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8[6T[1;36r[2;1H- **Requests** are what the scheduler reserves. The app is an idle Node.js process that answers small JSON requests, so 50m CPU and 64Mi cover it with margin. Small r(B[0;7m>[3;1H(B[m- **Memory limit 128Mi** is about 2x the typical resident size of a Node process. Node garbage-collects inside its heap, so a limit that is too tight gets the contain(B[0;7m>[4;1H(B[m- **CPU limit 200m** can throttle Node's startup, which uses more CPU than steady state. This may slow readiness on a cold start. I did not load-test these numbers, s(B[0;7m>[6;1H(B[0m[36m## What I deliberately skipped, and the risk[2;112H[39m(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8M[1;36r[2;1H[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[5T[1;36r[3;1H| | Request | Limit |[4d|---|---|---|[5d| CPU | 50m | 200m |[6d| Memory | 64Mi | 128Mi |[2d[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8[4T[1;36r[2;1Hcurl -H 'Host: demo.local' http://localhost/[2;55H# version is now 0.2.0[3d```[5d[36m## Resource requests and limits, and why[2;77H[39m(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8[4T[1;36r[2;1HChanging the app name or version on a running cluster:[4d```bash[5dhelm upgrade demo chart -n demo --reuse-values --set config.version=0.2.0[2;55H[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8[4T[1;36r[2;1Hhelm lint chart[3d(cd service && node --test)[4d```[2;16H[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8[3T[1;36r[2;3H| grep -E 'replicas:|APP_NAME|VERSION'[4d[36m# lint and unit tests[2;41H[39m(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8[3T[1;36r[3;1H[36m# override values (chart must follow)[4d[39m(B[mhelm template demo chart --set replicaCount=3 --set config.appName=shop --set config.version=9.9.9 \[2d[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8[2T[1;36r[2;1H[36m# two replicas answer: run several times, the "pod" value should vary[3d[39m(B[mfor i in 1 2 3 4; do curl -s -H 'Host: demo.local' http://localhost/ ; echo; done[2;70H[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[3T[1;36r[2;1Hcurl -H 'Host: demo.local' http://localhost/[2;55H# {"app":"demo-app","version":"0.1.0","pod":"..."}[3dcurl -H 'Host: demo.local' http://localhost/healthz   # {"status":"ok"}[2;105H[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8[2T[1;36r[3;1H[36m# service through the ingress[A[39m(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[2T[1;36r[2;1H[36m# cluster objects[3d[39m(B[mkubectl -n demo get deploy,pods,svc,ingress,configmap[2;18H[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8[2T[1;36r[3;1H```bash[A[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8[2T[1;36r[3;1H[36m## How to verify[A[39m(B[m[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8[2T[1;36r[2;1Hecho "127.0.0.1 demo.local" | sudo tee -a /etc/hosts[3d```[2;53H[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8[2T[1;36r[3;1H```bash[A[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8M[1;36r[2;1HOptional, to use the hostname in a browser or with plain `curl`:[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8[2T[1;36r[2;1H```[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8M[1;36r[2;1H./setup.sh[2;21H# second run must also exit 0 (idempotency)[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;34r8[2T[1;36r[2;1Hcd eb-devops-takehome[3d./setup.sh[3;21H# first run[2;22H[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8[3T[1;36r[3;1H```bash[4dgit clone https://github.com/Lokesh55raja/eb-devops-takehome.git[2d[?12l[?25h[?25l7[2;33r8[7T[1;36r[2;1Hlab/[2;19HPart 4 handout (fixes go in lab/broken-chart)[3dANSWERS.md[3;19HPart 5[4d```[6d[36m## How to run (Ubuntu)[8d[39m(B[mPrerequisites: Docker Engine (your user in the `docker` group), `kind`, `kubectl`, `helm`, `curl`. Ports 80 and 443 on the host must be free.[2;64H[?12l[?25h[?25l[36m# EB DevOps take-home[39m(B[m[K[3d[K[4dA small HTTP service, containerized, deployed to a local kind cluster with a Helm chart and a one-command setup script. Part 4 (the debug lab) lives in `lab/`.[6d**Status:** the service's unit tests pass. The Docker build, kind, Helm and `setup.sh` ran successfully on Ubuntu, and `helm lint` passes. Part 4 is in progress: 9 of(B[0;7m>[8;1H(B[m| Part | Status |[K[9d|---|---|[10d| 1. Service + Dockerfile | Code and 5 unit tests pass (`node --test`). Image built and ran on Ubuntu. |[11d| 2. Helm chart | `helm lint chart` passes. Overrides checked with `helm template`. Deployed on Ubuntu. |[12d| 3. `setup.sh` | Ran on Ubuntu, and a second run succeeded (idempotency checked). Ingress reachable at `demo.local`. |[13d| 4. Debug lab | 9 of 11 `verify` checks pass. Defects 1 to 6 fixed and written up in `lab/FINDINGS.md`. Reporter still open (Defect 7). |[14d| 5. ANSWERS.md | Rewritten in my own words. |[K[15d| 6. README | This file. |[17d[36m## Layout[39m(B[m[K[19;4H[K[20dsetup.sh          one-command kind + ingress-nginx + image + helm setup[21dservice/[21;19Happ.js, app.test.js, package.json, Dockerfile, .dockerignore[22dchart/[22;19HHelm chart: Deployment, Service, ConfigMap, Ingress[23dlab/[14X[23;19HPart 4 handout (fixes go in lab/broken-chart)[24dANSWERS.md[24;19HPart 5[25;4H[K[26d[K[27d[36m## How to run (Ubuntu)[39m(B[m[K[29dPrerequisites: Docker Engine (your user in the `docker` group), `kind`, `kubectl`, `helm`, `curl`. Ports 80 and 443 on the host must be free.[30d[K[31d```bash[K[32dgit clone https://github.com/Lokesh55raja/eb-devops-takehome.git[33dcd eb-devops-takehome[K[2;22H[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[?25l[?1